      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T11:13:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is wrong, the `temp` is a register and `Loadd()` expects an offset as the last argument. It is unfortunate that this actually compiles with the implicit conversion from `XRegister` to `int32_t`.\n\nThe correct sequence here would be\n\n    __ Sh3Add(temp, temp, method /* or `receiver_class` */);\n    __ Loadd(method, temp, vtable_offset);\n\nMoving the `vtable_offset` to the load instruction shortens the sequence.\n\n(I\u0027m not sure if you\u0027re still trying to avoid the \"Zba\" extension but I\u0027m willing to accept `shli+add` instead of `sh3add`.)",
      "range": {
